	<key>NSAppleEventsUsageDescription</key>
	<string>So that “alza il volume”, “metti in pausa” and “prossima canzone” reach Music and Spotify directly. Neko speaks to those two applications and to no others, with a fixed list of commands it can send.</string>
	<key>NSHumanReadableCopyright</key>
	<string>Public domain</string>
	<key>NSLocationUsageDescription</key>
	<string>So that “what is the weather” and “what is happening here” need no town named. Neko keeps the name of the town and of the region, never the coordinates.</string>
	<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>So that “what is the weather” and “what is happening here” need no town named. Neko keeps the name of the town and of the region, never the coordinates.</string>
	<key>NSMainNibFile</key>
